# Expo/React Native assume a flat node_modules: their packages resolve peers
# they never declare (@expo/metro-runtime -> whatwg-fetch, expo -> expo-modules-core,
# and so on through the graph). Under pnpm's isolated linker Metro fails on each
# in turn, so the workspace uses the hoisted layout Expo documents for pnpm.
#
# Trade-off accepted knowingly: hoisting also makes undeclared ("phantom")
# dependencies resolvable, so it is weaker than pnpm's default isolation. The
# typecheck gate in CI is what catches a package importing something it does
# not declare.
node-linker=hoisted

# apps/web + apps/admin are React 18; apps/mobile must be React 19 (RN 0.87).
# Hoisting nests the conflicting copy under the package that needs it, the same
# way npm workspaces do, so both versions coexist.
